      "text": "To find the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\), we first need to determine the lengths of \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\) based on the given distances \\( AB \\), \\( BC \\), and \\( AD \\).\n\nGiven:\n- \\( AB = 2 \\) units\n- \\( BC = 5 \\) units\n- \\( AD = 14 \\) units\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of \\( CD \\):\n\\[\nCD = BC + AB = 5 + 2 = 7 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the length of \\( AC \\):\n\\[\nAC = AB + BC = 2 + 5 = 7 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nThen, we calculate the length of \\( BD \\):\n\\[\nBD = BC + CD = 5 + 7 = 12 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\):\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio of } AC \\text{ to } BD = \\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{12}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}}\n\\]",
