      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\), we first need to determine the lengths of \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\).\n\nGiven:\n- \\(AB = 2\\) units\n- \\(BC = 5\\) units\n- \\(AD = 14\\) units\n\nSince points \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) lie on a line in that order, the distance \\(AC\\) can be calculated as:\n\\[\nAC = AB + BC = 2 + 5 = 7 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the length of \\(BD\\). Since \\(AD = 14\\) units and \\(AD\\) includes \\(AB\\) and \\(BC\\), the length of \\(BD\\) is:\n\\[\nBD = AD - AB = 14 - 2 = 12 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nNow, we have the lengths of \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\):\n\\[\nAC = 7 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\\[\nBD = 12 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nThe ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{12}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}}\n\\]",
